# What `vercel deploy` must never upload.
#
# The CLI does not read .gitignore. Without this file it uploads every file
# except a short built-in list, and that list excludes `.env.local` but not
# `.env` — so the server keys, and the migration-only management token, would
# travel with the source. Every rule in .gitignore is repeated here, so a CLI
# deployment uploads no more than git would track. Runtime configuration comes
# from the Vercel project's encrypted environment variables, never from a file.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

node_modules/
.next/
out/
coverage/
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo

.vercel/

test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright/

probes/out/

# supabase/.gitignore: local CLI link state. `.env` rules above already match
# its env files at any depth.
supabase/.branches/
supabase/.temp/
